Page actions: the Save bar's buttons without a card behind them

Every form page ends in Reset / Save / Save & Apply, which the theme docks to the bottom right
of the view. It drew them inside a frosted card of their own: a second border, a blurred
background and a large shadow around a row of buttons that already have their own surfaces.
On most pages that card is the only thing at the bottom of the view, so it read as a stray
box rather than as part of the page.

The card is gone: no background, border, blur, padding or shadow on the bar. The bar stays
sticky, so the buttons still float at the bottom right while the page scrolls, and each button
carries a soft shadow of its own so it stays legible over the content under it. In a modal the
bar keeps the footer strip the theme already gives it there, without the button shadows.

Applies to: https://github.com/anothaDev/luci-theme-vantage.git @ v1.2.0 (a7ff63b7), after 0001 and 0002.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

